<title>SWITZERLAND: Kuehne &amp; Nagel targets 70 mln sfr 1997 profit.</title>
<headline>Kuehne &amp; Nagel targets 70 mln sfr 1997 profit.</headline>
<dateline>SCHINDELLEGI, Switzerland 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>German-Swiss freight forwarding group Kuehne &amp; Nagel International AG is aiming for a 1997 profit of 70 million Swiss francs, excluding minority interests, finance chief Bruno Salzmann told reporters.  </p>
<p>He said cash flow could rise to 120 million Swiss francs from 110 million and that the company would maintain its pay-out ratio of 41 to 44 percent of profits.</p>
<p>The group boosted 1996 profit to 66.5 million from 59.2 million on turnover of 5.17 billion, up 2.1 percent.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
